The complete files preserve 1,590 topics and 3,221 directed prerequisite edges
unchanged from the pinned source. The source-derived index adds explicit,
limited activity references and candidate pattern routing; it does not change
the source graph or assert full-topic teaching/assessment. The original pattern
descriptions and priority recommendations are project planning. See
curriculum/README.md for provenance, file boundaries and rebuilding.

The runtime subset includes 87 topics and 92 relationships. It retains the original
math slice and adds limited science, data-display, English and computing activity matches
with direct prerequisites. Selection and removal of
age suffixes from topic names are described in the data and README.md.
No curriculum standards text is included. The application MIT license does
not supersede these licenses. The original stories and activities are authored
for this project.

The Paris puppet-post pack references Marble topic mt_VEwM7ClYYE for a
partial connection to arranging story events. Its central-message and full
retelling evidence are not assessed by this activity. The pack's story text
and its connection description are original.

